#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * Buyer app (confirmed with the person via mockup; English and Arabic, light and dark mode):
 *  - Home: the "Shopping for" car photo sits straight on the card (its PNG has its own shadow); All products / My car are raised buttons
 *    (the chosen one raised gold); the 8th section icon (All sections) is a raised gold button with a navy arrow;
 *  - Checkout: the steps box is raised, a warm cream gold in light mode and navy in dark mode (option B);
 *  - Add address: Search, Label, Recipient, (national address), Street, Postal code and Phone are set into the page;
 *  - Basket: a smaller - 2 +, its number and signs navy on the gold (also in dark mode);
 *  - Every product card: hold the photo for half a second and the product's other photos slide by (dots and "2 / 4"); letting go brings
 *    back the first one; a quick tap still opens the product.
 * Run it after patch-app-polish.
 *
 *   node scripts/patch-app-polish-2.js            dry run
 *   node scripts/patch-app-polish-2.js --write    applies it (each changed file is saved as <file>.before-app-polish-2 first)
 * Then: buyer app: q, then flutter run --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.0.210:4000   (No server change, no website change.)
 *
 * A file that is not as this patch expects is NOT changed (the whole patch stops; send that file). Windows (CRLF) line endings are handled.
 * Running it twice is harmless.
 */
